 "caveats": [
  "Product metrics come from the open-source fallback (no SciTools Understand license): 12 approximate metrics instead of 39, so BASE is not the paper's BASE.",
  "Exception-flow metrics come from JTratch without the authors' unpublished external-Javadoc file and without dependency jars: about 25% fewer possible exceptions than the authors' tool found on Hibernate 5.0.",
  "JTratch is not run-to-run deterministic: on ZooKeeper 3.6.0, repeated runs on identical sources changed 6 flow metrics in up to 76 of 161 files (catch/anti-pattern metrics never changed). Here the results use % Method Declaration, % Throw Statement, Avg # Declaring Methods, Avg Depth, Avg Max Depth, so the flow-metric findings (BSFC, SHAP) are conditional on this analyzer run.",
  "BSFC: the budget of 10 predictors (161 files / 15) forced a correlation cutoff of 0.240, which dropped BASE-significant # Bugs (pre). The authors' code behaves this way (it does not force them back), so BSFC vs BASE is not like-for-like here. This never happened on the paper's data.",
  "Tags and filters were chosen in the dashboard; check them against the project's release notes."
 ]
